        "tool_use_id": "call_3ad55493405e4157992a1847",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "## What is UseAgent?\n\nUseAgent (repo: `useagenthq/useagent`) describes itself as \"The open-source AI coworker for your team.\" It wraps AI coding agents — Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode (and Pi) — behind a single interface, giving each agent its own isolated cloud computer, your tools, and company context. Agents return finished deliverables rather than just answers: live websites, decks, spreadsheets, reports, and tested PRs.\n\n**How it works (key points from the README):**\n- Durable, event-sourced runs stored in Postgres — sessions survive backend restarts and stay inspectable\n- Each thread gets an isolated Linux sandbox (terminal, browser, noVNC desktop with MP4 recording); Daytona and Cube are the pluggable backends\n- A \"trusted gateway\" keeps credentials out of the sandbox; destructive tools pause for human approval via web or Slack\n- Slack-native (mention-to-run, threaded approvals), plus knowledge base, wiki, team memory, and versioned skills imported from `SKILL.md` files\n- Native artifact editing for DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, and PDF\n\n**Is it coding-focused?** Not exclusively. It runs coding agents, but it's positioned as a general-purpose team automation platform producing many work types (docs, decks, reports), with connectors for Gmail, Linear, Notion, and HubSpot alongside GitHub/Slack.\n\n**License:** AGPL-3.0-only, free for use and self-hosting; a separate commercial license is offered for proprietary embedding, OEM/white-label use, or non-AGPL distribution. Contributions require a CLA.\n\n**Launch/maturity info:** Status is alpha — \"expect rough edges, and APIs/schemas may change between releases,\" though it reportedly runs real daily workloads (pin a tag for stability). Runtime is Bun with Postgres 16+ and pgvector; self-hostable on any Linux host via Docker/Compose, including a one-command Hetzner Terraform setup. The repo shows ~151 stars, 18 forks, and 1,380 commits, with docs at useagent.org."
      }
    ]
  },
