        "tool_use_id": "call_e8cc982e1ca94b58ad07afad",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "## 49 Agents IDE — Summary\n\n**What it does:** 49 IDE (repo: `alpbahadur/49-IDE`) is an open-source, 2D agentic IDE that presents AI coding agents, terminals, git, Beads issue tables, Monaco editor, and markdown notes on a single zoomable infinite canvas. Its tagline: \"All agents. All terminals. All projects. All machines. One unified space.\"\n\n**How many agentic CLIs:** The README doesn't state a specific number — the \"49\" is the product name, not a CLI count. It's designed for \"AI agents in native CLIs\" generally, with Claude Code and Codex listed as repo topics, and features like per-pane Claude status and a HUD showing Claude API usage.\n\n**Platforms / access:**\n- Self-host locally via `./49ctl setup` and `./49ctl start`, then open `http://localhost:1071` (no account or login required)\n- Cluster hosting over Tailscale or LAN, or a hosted relay (app.49agents.com, \"coming soon\")\n- Any device — laptop, tablet, or phone — with the same workspace layout\n- A macOS desktop app (.dmg, runs as a tray icon; not notarized, so requires `xattr -cr` to unblock)\n\n**Key features:** Real tmux sessions via ttyd, broadcast typing to multiple terminals, zero-SSH multi-machine connection, live CPU/RAM/API overlay, git graph, permission notifications, and keyboard-first navigation (tab chords, WASD movement, number shortcuts).\n\n**License:** BSL 1.1 — \"free for individuals and small teams,\" converting to MIT on 2030-02-26."
      }
    ]
  },
